00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:18.255
- I don't know; I find in my career

00:07:18.255 --> 00:07:21.169
I've had a lot of people disagree with me.

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:23.037
(audience laughing)

00:07:23.037 --> 00:07:24.954
But I'm okay with that.

00:07:28.106 --> 00:07:30.349
I think that's part of the collaboration.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.655
It's like, I have to
understand what you're thinking

00:07:32.655 --> 00:07:35.901
and feeling if you're acting in a piece,

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:38.060
if you're the production designer.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.341
It's this collaboration of ideas,

00:07:40.341 --> 00:07:43.650
and as long as you know
that I'm always right.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.932
(audience laughing)

00:07:44.932 --> 00:07:46.680
It's great, it's perfect.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.367
- What happens if I don't know that?

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.755
- Then we have to talk longer.

00:07:50.755 --> 00:07:52.257
- Do you say, like let's meet in private?

00:07:52.257 --> 00:07:53.867
- Yeah, then we're
just, okay come with me,

00:07:53.867 --> 00:07:55.027
and let me just show you.

00:07:55.027 --> 00:07:56.438
- How do you shake it off,

00:07:56.438 --> 00:07:58.813
